#4471 was merged as one issue ("dates parse mm/dd in eu locales", status known) on the
assumption that all **412 reports** were a single bug. They are not. Running the desk's
own cause model (`causes.ts`: tenant locale + booking form + channel, never the intake
tag) over the 412 unique reports merged into #4471 gives two distinct problems:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Problem 1 — `parser` — 379 of 412 reports

The shared parser reads every date month-first, so tenants whose locale writes day-first
get day and month flipped. All 11 tenants on file are day-first (de-DE, es-ES, en-GB,
nl-NL, cs-CZ, it-IT, fr-FR, pl-PL, pt-PT, da-DK, en-IE), so all of them are affected
outside the booking-v3 form: app (204 reports), email (150), booking-v2 form (25).
First seen 2026-04-01, last seen 2026-10-04. Intake tagged 356 of these `parser` and 23
`hint`; the computed cause disagrees with the tag for 23 reports. Desk notes read 5 of
them as a one-day move (R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620), filed under this
cause.

Filed as a ticket in this repo: https://github.com/Bumshakalaka/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1

## Problem 2 — `hint` — 33 of 412 reports

The booking-v3 form prints an `MM/DD/YYYY` hint under the date field. The tenant's staff
type what the hint tells them, month first — but the form parses the entry the tenant's
day-first way, flipping day and month. A different bug from `parser`, and only the form
channel on booking-v3 tenants is affected: alder.physio (12 reports), copper.studio (11),
pale.harbour (10). First seen 2026-04-17, last seen 2026-09-22. Intake tagged 18 of these
`hint` and 15 `parser`.

Filed as a ticket in this repo: https://github.com/Bumshakalaka/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2

## Outcome (engineering update, desk)

#4471 was closed on 05 Oct. Per problem:

- `parser` — **fixed**: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`
- `hint` — **won't fix**: booking-v3 form retired

The tickets filed from this page were closed to match: the `parser` ticket as completed,
the `hint` ticket as not planned.


<Callout>
The merged ticket's own cause is `parser` (the majority, per `ticketCause`); the 33
`hint` reports were merged into the wrong place and need the ticket of their own.
</Callout>


